5251709},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see:\n- The farmers_markets data has states with their farmers market counts\n- The census data has SUMLEV=40 which is state-level data\n\nI need to:\n1. Sum the farmers_markets column from the farmers_markets table to get the total U.S. farmers markets\n2. Sum the POPESTIMATE2025 column from the census table (filtering for SUMLEV=40 for state-level data only) to get the total U.S. population in 2025\n3. Calculate: (total farmers markets / total population) * 100,000\n\nLet me create a build script that joins these two aggregates to compute the metric.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a build script to join the aggregated data and compute the metric:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01SWUvFwNwAM5rJ1RjSszZuC","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_metric.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read both sources\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"fm\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Aggregate: total farmers markets across all states\nfm_totals = fm.aggregate(\n    total_farmers_markets=fm.farmers_markets.sum()\n).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Aggregate: total population for state-level data (SUMLEV=40)\ncensus_totals = (\n    census.filter(census.SUMLEV == 40)\n    .aggregate(total_population=census.POPESTIMATE2025.sum())\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Join on constant key and compute metric\nexpr = (\n    fm_totals.join(census_totals, fm_totals.k == census_totals.k)\n    .mutate(\n        farmers_markets_per_100k=(\n            fm_totals.total_farmers_markets / census_totals.total_population * 100000\n        )\n    )\n    .select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"total_population\", \"farmers_markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":767,"cacheRead":16964,"cacheWrite":5273,"totalTokens":23018,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0038350000000000003,"cacheRead":0.0016964000000000003,"cacheWrite":0.00659125,"total":0.01213665},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":155},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915251710,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78M7yjhzA98dYQsN1Fn","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01SWUvFwNwAM5rJ1RjSszZuC","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1391 bytes to .xorq/scripts/build_metric.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915259128},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me build this metric script.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01TX846GKxezHLcM29syrB9s","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-81-q3v92zbn && xorq build .xorq/scripts/build_metric.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/bp_metric.txt && cat /tmp/bp_metric.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":138,"cacheRead":22237,"cacheWrite":807,"totalTokens":23195,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0006900000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0022237000000000003,"cacheWrite":0.00100875,"total":0.00393545},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":13},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915259128,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78MfLt89VXvtYHB2qwD","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01TX846GKxezHLcM29syrB9s","toolName":"bash","content":[{